<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Socialist Soviet Republic of Byelorussia</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1919 CE · capital Minsk</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Soviet Belarusian republic, proclaimed on 1 January 1919 and merged into Litbel within two months.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As German troops withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> at the end of 1918, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a>, displacing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belarusian-peoples-republic">Belarusian People's Republic</a>. On 1 January 1919 a Bolshevik conference in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> proclaimed the Socialist Soviet Republic of Byelorussia, partly to counter the nationalist government, and its leaders moved to Minsk.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its provisional government was headed by the writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zmitser-zhylunovich">Zmitser Zhylunovich</a>, known as Tsishka Hartny. The republic adopted a constitution at a congress of soviets in February 1919, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> soon cut off several eastern provinces and joined them directly to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>, leaving it only the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grodno">Grodno</a> regions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With Polish forces advancing, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> decided to merge the republic with the Lithuanian Soviet republic, and on 27 February 1919 it became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lithuanian-byelorussian-ssr">Lithuanian-Byelorussian SSR</a>. A Belarusian Soviet republic was proclaimed again in 1920 as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/byelorussian-ssr">Byelorussian SSR</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/socialist-soviet-republic-of-byelorussia.jpg" alt="Socialist Soviet Republic of Byelorussia" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Byelorussian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic_(1919%E2%80%931927).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Minsk</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zmitser Zhylunovich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Belarusian, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belarus">Belarus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>SSRB, First Byelorussian SSR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=socialist-soviet-republic-of-byelorussia" aria-label="Socialist Soviet Republic of Byelorussia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5291 327 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Socialist Soviet Republic of Byelorussia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5611 583L5820 533M5611 583L5556 562"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M5556 562h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5611 583h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5611 583h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Minsk. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=socialist-soviet-republic-of-byelorussia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
